---
title: Suliformes
---
# Suliformes

Suliformes is the order holding the cormorants of [[phalacrocoracidae]], the
gannets, the frigatebirds and the darters. All are seabirds with fully webbed
feet in which the hind toe is drawn forward into the web, and all take living
prey from open water. The group was split from the pelicans on molecular
evidence early in the present century, and the arrangement is still argued over
at the family level. Most species are colonial, and several plunge from height
while others pursue their quarry below the surface.
